    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44732" root="&#xA;                        ولع&#xA;                    " body-key="w1">
                        
                            4
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْلَعَهُ بِكَذَا</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He,</i> or <i>it, rendered him eagerly
desirous of such a thing;</i> or <i>fond of it.</i> (MA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْلَعَهُ بِهِ</span>
                        <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَغْرَاهُ بِهِ</span>. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَولِعَ بِهِ</span>
                        <i>He
became attached to it,</i> or <i>fond of it;</i> [<i>was
devoted,</i> or <i>addicted, to it; was eagerly desirous
of it;</i>] <i>he adhered, clung,</i> or <i>clave, to it;</i> or
<i>loved it;</i> (Msb;) <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُغْرِىَ به</span>. (S.) See
this last, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُغْرِمَ بِهِ</span>.

